  "description": "Change of use of the dwelling (Use Class C3) to a 6x bed HMO for up to 7 residents (Sui Generis) including addition of cycle and refuse storage  ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that this meets an identified need, and further would cause an increase in noise and disturbance to neighbouring properties thus presenting loss of local amenity. The site does not benefit from good access to public transport and is not considered a suitable location for an HMO.&nbsp;As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s housing supply and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)Policies&nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan&nbsp;(September 2024)"
  ],
